From 432cdb22f48ccdca6a960e06cdaf05293c3cd769 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:40:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] metrics: Service MetricsPort connections on a dedicated
 worker thread

When a relay's main libevent loop is saturated (for example during heavy
connection teardown or directory load), MetricsPort HTTP scrapes queued
behind mainloop events time out.

Follow the dnsserv_configure_listener() pattern in connection_listener_new()
to hand the CONN_TYPE_METRICS_LISTENER socket to a dedicated worker thread
in src/feature/metrics/metrics.c:
  - Poll the listener fd in metrics_worker_threadfn() and accept one
    MetricsPort client at a time using tor_accept_socket_nonblocking()
    (preserving Linux seccomp Sandbox 1 accept4() compatibility).
  - Temporarily release the listener's open-socket count slot during accept
    so MetricsPort remains reachable using the ULIMIT_BUFFER headroom even
    when the main thread reaches max_sockets - 1.
  - Synchronize SIGHUP/SETCONF listener replacement and shutdown via
    metrics_mutex and tor_event_loop_shutdown_is_pending().
